{"id":"l5","level":6,"levelName":"Reading literature","n":5,"of":5,"title":"Reading a real page","titleHe":"עַל הַסֵּפֶר","goal":"Put it together on unedited literary Hebrew.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Everything from here is reading. The shelf in the Browse tab is graded by how much of each book is built from the commonest two thousand words — start green and work down."},{"type":"text","body":"Three habits are worth carrying into it."},{"type":"tip","body":"Read to the end of the sentence before you look anything up. Hebrew's verb often arrives late, and half the words you'd have tapped resolve themselves once it does."},{"type":"tip","body":"When a word is unfamiliar, look for the three root letters first. Strip ו, ה, ב, ל, כ, מ, ש from the front and the endings from the back, and what's left is usually something you know."},{"type":"tip","body":"Unvocalized text is the norm outside textbooks and poetry. You'll read it faster than you expect, because context does the work the vowels were doing."}],"vocab":[{"he":"סוֹף","en":"end","translit":"sof"},{"he":"הַתְחָלָה","en":"beginning","translit":"hatchala"},{"he":"מִלָּה","en":"word","translit":"mila"},{"he":"מִשְׁפָּט","en":"sentence","translit":"mishpat"},{"he":"שֹׁרֶשׁ","en":"root","translit":"shoresh"},{"he":"מַשְׁמָעוּת","en":"meaning","translit":"mashma'ut"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["correct","to, towards","and he said","end"],"correct":3,"prompt":"סוֹף","translit":"sof"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["don't (with the future)","beginning","also","to me"],"correct":1,"prompt":"הַתְחָלָה","translit":"hatchala"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["two (m.)","word","maybe","book"],"correct":1,"prompt":"מִלָּה","translit":"mila"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["sentence","door","seems, looks","his house"],"correct":0,"prompt":"מִשְׁפָּט","translit":"mishpat"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["root","on me, about me","heart","tea"],"correct":0,"prompt":"שֹׁרֶשׁ","translit":"shoresh"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["sun","hard, difficult","to, for","meaning"],"correct":3,"prompt":"מַשְׁמָעוּת","translit":"mashma'ut"},{"type":"match","pairs":[["סוֹף","end"],["שֹׁרֶשׁ","root"],["הַתְחָלָה","beginning"],["מִלָּה","word"],["מַשְׁמָעוּת","meaning"]]},{"type":"read","he":"מִלָּה","translit":"mila","en":"word"},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["סוֹף","מִלָּה","מִשְׁפָּט","מַשְׁמָעוּת"],"correct":0,"say":"סוֹף","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “word”?","options":["מַכִּיר","בֵּין","מִלָּה","אֶתְמוֹל"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “end”?","options":["הַיּוֹם","סוֹף","מִצְטַעֵר","אֶחָד"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “root”?","options":["שָׁבוּעַ","יָכוֹל","שֹׁרֶשׁ","נוֹסֵעַ"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “sentence”?","options":["כַּדּוּרֶגֶל","מִשְׁפָּט","לַיְלָה","קוֹרֵא"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “root” in Hebrew","answer":"שֹׁרֶשׁ","hint":"shoresh"}]}